\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. At even, ere the sun was set,
\par The sick, O Lord, around Thee lay;
\par O in what divers pains they met!
\par O with what joy they went away!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Once more 'tis eventide, and we,
\par Oppressed with various ills, draw near;
\par What if Thy form we cannot see?
\par We know and feel that Thou art here.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. O Saviour Christ, our woes dispel:
\par For some are sick, and some are sad,
\par And some have never loved Thee well,
\par And some have lost the love they had.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. And some have found the world is vain,
\par Yet from the world they break not free;
\par And some have friends who give them pain,
\par Yet have not sought a friend in Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. And all, O Lord, crave perfect rest,
\par And to be wholly free from sin;
\par And they who fain would serve Thee best
\par Are conscious most of wrong within.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. O Saviour Christ, Thou too art Man;
\par Thou hast been troubled, tempted, tried;
\par Thy kind but searching glance can scan
\par The very wounds that shame would hide.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. Thy touch has still its ancient power;
\par No word from Thee can fruitless fall:
\par Hear in this solemn evening hour,
\par And in Thy mercy heal us all.
\par                               Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

